Layout
------
Data qubits (3 blocks of 3):
  block 1: D0, D1, D2
  block 2: D3, D4, D5
  block 3: D6, D7, D8

Z-stabilizers (intra-block weight-2):
  Z_1 = Z0 Z1   (anc 9)
  Z_2 = Z1 Z2   (anc 10)
  Z_3 = Z3 Z4   (anc 11)
  Z_4 = Z4 Z5   (anc 12)
  Z_5 = Z6 Z7   (anc 13)
  Z_6 = Z7 Z8   (anc 14)

X-stabilizers (inter-block weight-6):
  X_1 = X0 X1 X2 X3 X4 X5   (anc 15)
  X_2 = X3 X4 X5 X6 X7 X8   (anc 16)

Logical operators (verified to commute with all 8 stabs, anticommute with each other):
  Z_L = X0 X1 X2     (Shor logical Z; first block's X-product)
  X_L = Z0 Z3 Z6     (Shor logical X; one Z per block)

Circuit (in execution order)
----------------------------
PASS 1 (encoding, 9 gates):
  H(0); CNOT(0,1); CNOT(1,2)        // block 1 GHZ-3
  H(3); CNOT(3,4); CNOT(4,5)        // block 2 GHZ-3
  H(6); CNOT(6,7); CNOT(7,8)        // block 3 GHZ-3

PASS 2 (syndrome measurement, 8 ancilla read):
  Z-stab gadgets (6): for each Z_k = Z_i Z_j with anc a:
    CNOT(i, a); CNOT(j, a)
  X-stab gadgets (2): for each X_k = X_i ... with anc a:
    H(a); CNOT(a, i_1); ... CNOT(a, i_6); H(a)
  Measure all 8 ancillae into creg_syn[0..7]
    syn[0..5] = Z_1..Z_6
    syn[6..7] = X_1, X_2

PASS 3 (logical Z destructive readout, 9 data measurements):
  H(0); H(1); H(2)                  // rotate block 1 to X basis for Z_L = X0X1X2
  Measure D0..D8 -> creg_dat[0..8]
  Z_L = dat[0] XOR dat[1] XOR dat[2]    // 0 = logical |0_L>

